hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15537","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Damrah al-Fazari narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Sulayt, from his father Abu Sulayt, he said: The prohibition of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against eating the flesh of domestic donkeys came to us while the pots were boiling with them, so we overturned them upon their faces."
"15538","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah said: And I heard, I, from Ibn Abi Shaybah, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Damrah al-Fazari, from Abdullah ibn Abi Sulayt, from his father Abu Sulayt, and he was a Badri, he said: The prohibition of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against the flesh of donkeys came to us while we were at Khaybar, so we overturned them, though we were hungry."
